<lem-type Note extends Page>
  topic: string
  layout: (Note, html): html = note
</lem-type>

<lem-fn note(n: Note, body: html)>
  <h1><lem.n.topic></h1>
  <p><lem.page.url></p>
  <lem.body>
</lem-fn>

A `layout` default names a function; it does not call it. `note` reads `page`, which
the render binds and the loader never does — and that is the render's business, not the
load order's, so the schema links.
